whether these measurements refer to the bezel/engraved field, overall plate, or 
include the hoop.)  
   - The “Key takeaways” also summarize that the paper confirms the ring’s 
authenticity, counters earlier claims of forgery from the 1920s, identifies the 
so‑called “watch-dog” or “dragon” figure as a scorpion (an apotropaic Bronze Age
symbol), and relates this iconographic reinterpretation to the wider argument 
about the ring’s meaning and authenticity.

