{"query": {"id": "20260628165813025125_4fc31aa0", "handle": "q1", "text": 
"\"Ring of Nestor\" museum catalogue gold", "importance": "supporting"}, 
"items": [{"id": "20260628165853300815_712b60a2", "type": "Evidence", "text": 
"The catalogue entry lists the title as: \"The ring of Nestor : a glimpse into 
the Minoan after-world and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and 
bead-seals from Thisbe / by Sir Arthur Evans.\"", "source_ids": 
["20260628165852367169_e90ea132"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628165853383233_5005b69a", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The catalogue 
classifies the work under subjects including Minoan civilization, gold 
signet-rings, and sepulchral treasure from Thisbe, Boeotia.", "source_ids": 
["20260628165852367169_e90ea132"], "citations": [1]}, {"id": 
"20260628165853477136_f9253fa6", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The Journal of 
Hellenic Studies article is titled: \"'The Ring of Nestor': A Glimpse into the 
Minoan After-World and A Sepulchral Treasure of Gold Signet-Rings and Bead-Seals
from Thisbê, Boeotia\" and is credited to Sir Arthur Evans.", "source_ids": 
["20260628165852403005_c0352755"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628165853587978_541fe924", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The journal 
metadata lists the article as originally published in 1925, with an online 
publication date noted as 23 December 2013.", "source_ids": 
["20260628165852403005_c0352755"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628165853694162_b7edcdd6", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The article 
description states that it discusses a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings 
and bead-seals from Thisbê in Boeotia, focusing on the object Evans calls the 
\"Ring of Nestor\" as central to his interpretation of Minoan beliefs about the 
afterworld.", "source_ids": ["20260628165852403005_c0352755"], "citations": 
[2]}, {"id": "20260628170105918805_640befc6", "type": "Claim", "text": "Sir 
Arthur Evans authored a study titled \"The Ring of Nestor: A Glimpse into the 
Minoan After-World and a Sepulchral Treasure of Gold Signet-Rings and Bead-Seals
from Thisbe (Thisbê), Boeotia,\" which focuses on a gold signet ring he calls 
the \"Ring of Nestor\" and a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and 
bead-seals from Thisbe in Boeotia, in relation to Minoan conceptions of the 
afterworld.", "source_ids": ["20260628165852367169_e90ea132", 
"20260628165852403005_c0352755"], "citations": [1, 2]}, {"id": 
"20260628170106382047_409afa3a", "type": "Claim", "text": "Evans’s article \"The
Ring of Nestor\" on the sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals 
from Thisbe (Thisbê), Boeotia, was originally published in 1925 and later made 
available online by Cambridge University Press on 23 December 2013.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628165852403005_c0352755"], "citations": [2]}, {"id": 
"20260628171004909866_886a7c0e", "type": "Claim", "text": "Sir Arthur Evans 
authored a study titled \"The Ring of Nestor: A Glimpse into the Minoan 
After-World and a Sepulchral Treasure of Gold Signet-Rings and Bead-Seals from 
Thisbê, Boeotia,\" focusing on a particular gold signet ring he designated as 
the \"Ring of Nestor\" within a sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and 
bead-seals from Thisbe in Boeotia.", "source_ids": 
["20260628165852367169_e90ea132", "20260628165852403005_c0352755"], "citations":
[1, 2]}, {"id": "20260628171005417840_8c777538", "type": "Claim", "text": 
"Evans’s study interprets the imagery on the gold signet ring known as the 
\"Ring of Nestor\" as providing insight into Minoan conceptions of the 
afterworld and related funerary or religious beliefs.", "source_ids": 
["20260628165852367169_e90ea132", "20260628165852403005_c0352755"], "citations":
[1, 2]}, {"id": "20260628171005675201_c91baf5f", "type": "Claim", "text": "The 
article \"The Ring of Nestor: A Glimpse into the Minoan After-World and a 
Sepulchral Treasure of Gold Signet-Rings and Bead-Seals from Thisbê, Boeotia\" 
by Sir Arthur Evans was originally published in the Journal of Hellenic Studies 
in 1925 and its digital version was made available online by Cambridge 
University Press on 23 December 2013.", "source_ids": 
["20260628165852403005_c0352755"], "citations": [2]}], "offset": 0, "limit": 40,
"total": 10, "next_offset": null}
