"source_ids": ["20260628170043086880_97dad9bd"], "citations": [3]}, {"id": 
"20260628170409234221_8664553f", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The iconography 
paper is described as comparing '人物姿态、神灵形象、自然元素等' (figural poses,
divine figures, natural elements) on the Ring of Nestor with known 
Minoan–Mycenaean seal imagery to test conformity to period styles.", 
"source_ids": ["20260628170043086880_97dad9bd"], "citations": [3]}, {"id": 
"20260628170409326377_b876aec5", "type": "Evidence", "text": "The snippet notes 
that the paper recounts an 'acceptance history' in which the ring was initially 
viewed as a Late Minoan high‑rank funerary object and later became the subject 
